diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Dynamic routing on router0 (FRR/RIP). Hosts in the CS (192.168.2.0/24) and IT (192.168.1.0/24) LANs rely on router0 to reach other zones.

Mechanism: From cs_lab1 and it_hod, pings to the Server Room (1.0.0.x) return “From 192.168.2.1/192.168.1.1 Destination Net Unreachable,” proving router0 has no route to those networks. Router0’s routing table contains only connected routes (192.168.1.0/24, 192.168.2.0/24, 10.0.0.0/8) with no learned routes to 1.0.0.0/8 or 128.168.0.0/16. Meanwhile, router1 and router2 are exchanging RIP routes and can reach each other and the Internet Lab/Server Room, matching the observation that other zones still intercommunicate.

Localization: Router0, process-level. frr.
